; The lowered `(sugar-normal :a 1)` fails normal validation because
; sugar-normal declares `:a` as a string. Re-validation surfaces
; wrong_underlying on the lowered tree; the provenance side-table
; lets a downstream consumer trace the lowered form back to the
; source `(sugar :a 1)`.
(diagnostics
  (diagnostic :code wrong_underlying :path [sugar-normal a]))
